  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nLingering showers within a deformation zone to the northwest of\na slow-moving closed low will slowly wane this morning. \nEasterly downsloping flow will support low-level drying and \nerosion of as sfc high pressure builds.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nAmid strengthening sfc high pressure, below-normal temperature\nwill be likely thru the weekend. Thu night in particular will\nfeature the coldest temperature with values broadly approaching\nthe low-mid 40s, and potentially into the 30s in Canaan Valley,\nwhere frost may develop locally in typical cold spots.\n\nAs high pressure advances eastward, and flow aloft transitions\ntoward westerly/southwesterly, temperature trends seem likely to\nreturn toward normal (maxima in the low 70s and minima in the \nlow 50s).\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\nEnsemble trends away from weekend precipitation associated with\nstrengthening coastal low pressure have continued.\n\nThe next potential for rain appears to be in the Tue-Wed \ntimeframe, when a trough amplifies across the Upper OH Valley. \nAt this time, buoyancy appears meager, so potential for \nhazardous weather appears low despite a stronger wind field.",
